==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*fleuganą}}. Cognate with Old English {{m|ang|fleogan|flēoġan}} (Modern English {{m|en|fly}}), Old Frisian {{m|ofs|fliaga|fliāga}} (Saterland Frisian {{m|stq|fljooge}}), Old Saxon {{m|osx|fliogan}} (Low German {{m|nds|flegen}}), Old Dutch {{m|odt|fliogan}} (Dutch {{m|nl|vliegen}}), Old High German {{m|goh|fliogan}} (German {{m|de|fliegen}}), Gothic {{m|got|𐌸𐌻𐌹𐌿𐌲𐌰𐌽}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{m|ine-pro|*pleuk-}}. Indo-European cognates include Lithuanian {{m|lt|plaukti|plaũkti}}.

===Verb===
{{non-verb|flaug|flugu|floginn}}

# to [[fly]]

